        "math_academy_id": "q-102837",
        "problem": "If $\\overset{\u2015}{P}={{3}^{5},{3}^{7},{3}^{8}}$ and $\\overset{\u2015}{Q}={{3}^{6},{3}^{8},{3}^{9},{3}^{10}},$ then what is $\\overset{\u2015}{P\\cap Q}?$",
        "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{P\\cap Q}\u2261\\overset{\u2015}{P}\\cup \\overset{\u2015}{Q}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{P\\cap Q} & =\\overset{\u2015}{P}\\cup \\overset{\u2015}{Q} \\\\  & ={{3}^{5},{3}^{7},{3}^{8}}\\cup {{3}^{6},{3}^{8},{3}^{9},{3}^{10}} \\\\  & ={{3}^{5},{3}^{6},{3}^{7},{3}^{8},{3}^{9},{3}^{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
